35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,The firms flagged clay and slippage. That is a major risk for deep digging. I need to know if the plans avoid that.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The eastern avenue trees died because watering was ignored. We cannot propose planting without a guaranteed aftercare contract.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,"The roll is down to seven people. That is very few. But the volunteers are still there, helping on weekends.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The basin held, but the apron failed. Planted ground costs triple to maintain. I need to see which plans avoid that trap.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The ledger shows planted ground costs triple to maintain. With only seven staff left, that gap is widening. I worry about the long-term burden.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Minako, triple costs are scary. But the depot notes say we can hoard the south in stages. That keeps the park open while we work.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, triple costs confirm the risk. The crossing data shows people stick to hard ground. We must design for that reality, not idealism.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, I see. But the volunteers are so kind. Maybe they can help with the watering? I hope the seven staff are not too tired.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, volunteers are a bonus, not a plan. I need to see which candidates minimize the high-cost planted areas.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, you are right. Volunteers cannot replace the budget. I need to see which plans keep the hard surfaces dominant to control those rising costs.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, the clay risk means we must avoid deep cuts. The phasing notes say the centre cannot be hoarded. That is a tight constraint for any major dig.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the clay is a hard limit. The crossing data shows people already avoid soft ground. We must design for the path, not the pit.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Kenji, that sounds difficult. I hope the seven staff are not too tired. The volunteers are very kind, but they are not enough for everything.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Kenji, the clay risk is real. But the apron failure shows that even hard surfaces decay without proper maintenance. We must prioritize durability over aesthetics.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Kenji, the clay risk is real. But my concern is the upkeep. If we dig deep, the maintenance burden grows. I need to see which plans keep the hard surfaces dominant to control those rising costs.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Minako, durability is key. I will check the condition of works from the earlier programme to see what actually survived the last decade.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, durability is the only honest metric. I will check the drainage callouts to see how the ground actually handles the rain.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,"@Minako, I agree. I just hope the volunteers can help with the small things. I am worried the staff are too tired to do it all.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, drainage is vital, but the apron failure proves that even hard surfaces decay without proper maintenance. We must prioritize durability over aesthetics.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, I agree. Durability is essential. I will check the drainage callouts to see how the ground handles rain, which directly impacts long-term upkeep costs.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
