60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, the clay risk is critical. Candidate A reshapes drainage, which means deep digging. That is a no-go for me.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, agreed. A is a recipe for failure. The crossing data shows people want firm ground, not mud. B’s paved square fits that reality perfectly.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, the paved square sounds nice. But who will sweep it every day? I worry the seven staff are already so tired.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, the paved square is hard surface. My data shows that costs a third of planted ground. It is the most sustainable option for our budget.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, that aligns with my ledger findings. Hard surfaces are far cheaper to maintain. I am strongly leaning toward B to protect the city’s long-term finances.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Minato, the terraces in D are on the south. The depot notes say we can hoard that in stages. It keeps the park open while we work.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the south is the right place. The crossing data shows people already favor firm ground. D’s hard surfaces match how the park is actually used, not how we wish it were.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, the running loop sounds fun. But who will clean the courts? I hope the volunteers can help with the small things, but I am worried the staff are too tired.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, D’s hard surfaces are cheaper, but the courts and changing rooms are complex. My data shows complex structures decay faster. B’s simple paving is more durable.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, I agree. The changing rooms in D add complexity and upkeep. B’s simple paving is far cheaper to maintain. I am leaning toward B to protect the city’s long-term finances.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Minako, the changing rooms are a maintenance trap. D is simpler than A, but B is the safest bet for the ground.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, complexity is the enemy. D’s courts and changing rooms are a liability. B’s simple paving respects the ground and the staff. I am leaning toward B.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minato,,"@Minako, I understand. The simple paving is good. But I worry about the staff. If B is chosen, will the seven people be enough to keep it clean?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, the simple paving is low-maintenance. The apron failed due to neglect, not complexity. B is the most durable choice for our current staffing levels.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, the simple paving is low-maintenance. With only seven staff, B is the only option that won’t bankrupt the city in three years. I am ready to vote.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, I agree. B avoids the clay risk and the deep digging. The simple paving is the safest choice for the ground and the schedule. I am ready to vote.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, agreed. B respects the ground and the people. It is the only plan that survives contact with reality. I am ready to vote.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minato,,"@Minako, thank you for explaining. I am still a little worried about the tired staff, but I trust the simple paving is easier. I am ready to vote.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, I am ready to vote. B is the only plan that respects the data and our limited resources.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, I agree. B is the only plan that respects the ledger and our limited staff. I am ready to vote.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
